{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$f(x)$ is the product of two, more basic, expressions: $\\sin(x)$ and $x^{-2}$.\n\nTherefore, the derivative of $f$ can be found using **the product rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)v(x)]\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)+u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=u'(x)v(x)+u(x)v'(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}f'(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\sin(x)x^{-2}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\sin(x)\\right]x^{-2}+\\sin(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[x^{-2}]\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The product rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\cos(x)x^{-2}+\\sin(x)(-2)x^{-3}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }\\sin(x)\\text{ and }x^{-2}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{\\cos(x)}{x^2}-\\dfrac{2\\sin(x)}{x^3}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$f'(x)=\\dfrac{\\cos(x)}{x^2}-\\dfrac{2\\sin(x)}{x^3}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=\\sin(x)x^{-2}$.\n\n**Find $f'(x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{\\cos(x)}{x^2}-\\dfrac{2\\sin(x)}{x^3}$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\dfrac{\\cos(x)}{x^2}-\\dfrac{2\\sin(x)}{x}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{\\sin(x)}{x^2}-\\dfrac{2\\cos(x)}{x^3}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{\\sin(x)}{x^2}-\\dfrac{2\\cos(x)}{x}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
